  "solution": {
    "text": "Lattice energy <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">α</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mo>-</mo></msub></mrow></mfrac></math><br />With a small anion as <mrow><mi></mi></mrow><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></math>, the lattice energy decreases more rapidly along a series of salts with increasing cation size and thus solubility increases<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>LiF</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>NaF</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>KF</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>RbF</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>CsF</mi></math>",
